      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\"><span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span><span class=\"time\">25 min</span><span class=\"chip warn\">Medium</span><span class=\"chip accent\">2-string DP grid</span><a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/interleaving-string/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 97</a></div>\n  <h1>Interleaving String</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Insight in one line: if s3 is an interleaving, its first i + j characters always use exactly i characters of s1 and j of s2, so the state is just (i, j); cell (i, j) is reachable from above when s1's i-th character matches and from the left when s2's j-th matches. O(m &times; n) time, O(n) memory with one row.</p>\n"
  },
